body:
Three independent bugs causing incorrect or missing CVD data: Binance's `www.binance.com/fapi` klines endpoint is blocked on Vercel, the first CVD row per exchange was always seeded with `0`, and existing rows with `cvd=0` never fell back to `buy_volume - sell_volume`.

## Changes

- **`api/futures-exchange.js`** — Replace blocked `www.binance.com` klines block with `fapi.binance.com` endpoints:
  - `ticker/24hr` → price (required)
  - `openInterest` → OI (required)
  - `takerBuySellVol` → `cvdDelta` with graceful fallback to ticker-derived estimate
  - `topLongShortPositionRatio` → long/short split with graceful fallback to 50/50

- **`api/cron-collect-cvd.js`** — Seed row no longer discards actual buy pressure; use `data.buyVolume - data.sellVolume` when no previous row exists:
  ```js
  // before
  const intervalDelta = prevRow ? ... : 0;
  // after
  const intervalDelta = prevRow ? ... : data.buyVolume - data.sellVolume;
  ```

- **`api/get-history.js`** — `Number.isFinite(0)` is `true`, so rows stored with `cvd=0` were short-circuiting the `buy_volume - sell_volume` fallback:
  ```js
  // before
  const delta = Number.isFinite(record.cvd) ? record.cvd : ...;
  // after
  const delta = (Number.isFinite(record.cvd) && record.cvd !== 0) ? record.cvd : ...;
  ```

