<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> Fix three bugs in proffessa/xrp-cvd-tracker. Make ALL three changes in a single PR.
> 
> ## Fix 1: api/futures-exchange.js — Binance klines endpoint is blocked on Vercel
> 
> The current code in the binance block calls:
>   https://www.binance.com/fapi/v1/klines?symbol=XRPUSDT&interval=5m&limit=2
> 
> This returns null (blocked). Replace the entire binance block so it:
> 1. Uses `fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/ticker/24hr?symbol=XRPUSDT` as the primary price+volume source
> 2. Uses `fapi.binance.com/futures/data/takerBuySellVol?symbol=XRPUSDT&period=5m&limit=1` for cvdDelta (optional, fallback to ticker estimate)
> 3. Uses `fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/openInterest?symbol=XRPUSDT` for OI
> 4. Uses `fapi.binance.com/futures/data/topLongShortPositionRatio?symbol=XRPUSDT&period=5m&limit=1` for long/short (optional)
> 
> Replace the binance block with:
> 
> ```javascript
> if (exchange === 'binance') {
>   const [takerJson, oiJson, lsJson, tickerJson] = await Promise.all([
>     safeFetchWithFallback([
>       'https://fapi.binance.com/futures/data/takerBuySellVol?symbol=XRPUSDT&period=5m&limit=1',
>     ]),
>     safeFetchWithFallback([
>       'https://fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/openInterest?symbol=XRPUSDT',
>     ]),
>     safeFetchWithFallback([
>       'https://fapi.binance.com/futures/data/topLongShortPositionRatio?symbol=XRPUSDT&period=5m&limit=1',
>     ]),
>     safeFetchWithFallback([
>       'https://fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/ticker/24hr?symbol=XRPUSDT',
>     ]),
>   ]);
> 
>   if (!tickerJson) throw new Error('binance: ticker/24hr endpoint failed');
>   if (!oiJson) throw new Error('binance: openInterest endpoint failed');
> 
>   let cvdDelta;
>   if (takerJson && takerJson[0]) {
>     const latest = takerJson[0];
>     cvdDelta = parseFloat(latest.buyVol) - parseFloat(latest.sellVol);
>   } else {
>     const vol = parseFloat(tickerJson.volume);
>     const priceChangePercent = parseFloat(tickerJson.priceChangePercent) / 100;
>     const buyRatio = Math.max(0.4, Math.min(0.6, 0.5 + priceChangePercent * 0.5));
>     cvdDelta = (vol * (buyRatio - (1 - buyRatio))) / 288;
>   }
> 
>   const openInterest = parseFloat(oiJson.openInterest);
>   let longVol, shortVol;
>   if (lsJson && lsJson[0]) {
>     longVol = openInterest * parseFloat(lsJson[0].longAccount);
>     shortVol = openInterest * parseFloat(lsJson[0].shortAccount);
>   } else {
>     longVol = openInterest * 0.5;
>     shortVol = openInterest * 0.5;
>   }
>   const price = parseFloat(tickerJson.lastPrice);
> 
>   data = { cvdDelta, openInterest, longVol, shortVol, price };
> }
> ```
> 
> ## Fix 2: api/cron-collect-cvd.js — seed row intervalDelta is 0
> 
> Change line:
> ```javascript
> const intervalDelta = prevRow
>   ? (data.buyVolume - data.sellVolume) - (prevRow.buy_volume - prevRow.sell_volume)
>   : 0;
> ```
> 
> To:
> ```javascript
> const intervalDelta = prevRow
>   ? (data.buyVolume - data.sellVolume) - (prevRow.buy_volume - prevRow.sell_volume)
>   : data.buyVolume - data.sellVolume;
> ```
> 
> ## Fix 3: api/get-history.js — delta is always 0 for existing rows because cvd===0 short-circuits the fallback
> 
> Change:
> ```javascript
> const delta = Number.isFinite(record.cvd)
>   ? record.cvd
>   : (record.buy_volume || 0) - (record.sell_volume || 0);
> ```
> 
> To:
> ```javascript
> const delta = (Number.isFinite(record.cvd) && record.cvd !== 0)
>   ? record.cvd
>   : (record.buy_volume || 0) - (record.sell_volume || 0);
> ```
> 


</details>



